\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{CJKutf8}
\title{Maritime Trade and the Ming Sea Ban: A Reassessment}
\author{L.~Wang}
\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\begin{CJK}{UTF8}{gbsn}
\section{引言}
明代中期的海禁政策长期被视为王朝保守性的象征，既有研究多从朝贡体制的角度加以解释。
然而，近年出土的沿海商帮账簿显示，隆庆开关之前的私人海上贸易规模远超官方记录。
本文利用新整理的泉州、宁波两地档案，重新估算嘉靖至万历年间民间出海商船的数量变化。
我们的估计表明，海禁最严厉的年份反而对应着走私贸易的峰值。这个结果挺让人意外的，说明海禁确实把民间贸易给逼到地底下去了。
\end{CJK}
\section{Historiography}
Earlier scholarship treated the sea ban as a simple expression of
dynastic conservatism, and the tribute system supplied the
interpretive frame for most accounts of Ming maritime policy.
The archival turn of the past decade has complicated that picture:
private trade did not vanish under prohibition but changed its
organisation, its routes, and its relationship to local officials.
\section{Conclusion}
The reassessment suggests that prohibition reshaped rather than
suppressed maritime commerce along the south-eastern coast.
\end{document}

